qemu-experimental
=================

QEMU patches from work on the SPARC64 sun4v (UltraSPARC T1 / "niagara") target:
getting an OpenSPARC hypervisor, OpenBoot and Solaris to run under QEMU, and
fixing what breaks along the way.

The split is by destination, and it is the only thing that decides where a patch
lives:

  upstream/   posted to qemu-devel, or written intending to. Numbered as a
              series. These are meant to stop existing here once accepted --
              0001 already did, landing as commit 76dbe26fd6.

  devel/      published because it is useful to anyone doing the same work, but
              deliberately not proposed upstream. Typically models a device or
              exposes state that only matters when building or modifying sun4v
              firmware.

Each directory carries a SHA256SUMS covering its patches. A patch here is
byte-identical to the working tree it was developed and tested in.

Applying
--------
Patches are against qemu.git master and are developed against a fresh clone each
time, so record the base commit when reporting a result. As of the last update
the base was 3e3ccab106 (v11.1.0-rc3).

    git clone https://gitlab.com/qemu-project/qemu.git
    cd qemu
    patch -p1 < .../upstream/0002-target-sparc-fix-sun4v-TTE-page-size-truncation-32M-256M-pages.patch
    patch -p1 < .../devel/niagara-hvuart-console.patch
    mkdir ../build && cd ../build
    ../qemu/configure --target-list=sparc64-softmmu --enable-debug && make -j"$(nproc)"

The two are independent: 0002 fixes page-size decoding and matters for any sun4v
guest using 32M/256M pages; the hvuart patch matters only if you run firmware you
built yourself.
